Z||000010||Xtreme Fiero's||10-31-2000||08:07 PM||||Is Maryland perf. Coatings part of Maryland Performance Center? Where is the EGR flange?<p>[This message has been edited by Xtreme Fiero's (edited 10-31-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||HYPTNOTiSE||10-31-2000||09:08 PM||||No Maryland performance coatings is not part of Maryland performance center. But i'm in good with maryland performance center too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I'm going to be doing all my tuning on their new chassis dyno as soon as my engines in. My buddy's dad owns the place.  I dumped EGR a long time ago, but is also available on these headers, but i dont think it's neccesary.   The headers are available for sale, but i wouldn't say they're affordable.  They take about 2-3 weeks to make, and are tig welded inside and out, and are done by hand with great care. They're available with and without egr, 02 bungs, and thermal coating. Available for manual and auto. N/A and turbo.<P>------------------<BR>       Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ Nitrous<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tcac.net/~daddyg/hypsig.gif"> ||||reg||1
