Z||000014||Xtreme Fiero's||10-31-2000||10:50 PM||||HYPTNOTiSE: I'm very bad with names but good w/ cars Hunter Green Cougar right? Black Gost stripe, He is at my work every day. Last time I spoke to him he was geting ready to put it a fancy roll cage or something like that. Sweet car<P>how much would it cost to get the headers W/ the EGR & O2 bung and coated($650-800?)? How hard is it to dissable the EGR system and what it the point? and finaly could I add a Y pipe with a Turbo flange later, How much is that and would/ could it work with stock manifolds? ||||reg||1
Z||000015||Shaun41178||10-31-2000||10:52 PM||||All I can say is that those headers look so much better in person.  Those pics don't do it justice.  Diameter on thos headers are huge.  They won't be choking top end at all.  I went and picked up the headers with Mike and I needed someone to tie a cup under my chin to collect all the druel.  Awesome Headers.  Equeal length or damn near close to it.<P>Yea people those headers are expensive but they will outflow any other headers for a Fiero I am sure.  If you think Fiero Stores are expensive or that Fiero Heavens were expensive then you can't afford these either.  Mike paid a good penny but will flow well and needed them for his engine application.  In the future I plan on having hyptnotise(Mike) provide me with a set of headers for a turbo application.  That is at least 2 years away though.<P>Yea that is me in the background of the last pic.  That pics helps to show just how large the headers are.  Oh yea for you female forum members, ain't I cute?<P>I would like to thank Mike for having me at his place for the weekend and also for the 2.8 crank with DIS wheel, set of rods, and a pair of aluminum heads.  The heads and crank are for my all aluminum build up I plan on doing in the future.  Thanks again Mike.<BR>||||reg||14
